# The vendored upstream licences are copies, and `notices/upstream/README.md`
# says they are copied byte for byte. On Windows, Git's line-ending conversion
# would quietly make that untrue — the file checked out is not the file that was
# fetched, and an attribution that has been reformatted is exactly what vendoring
# these instead of rendering a template was meant to avoid.
#
# This is the same trap 0.13.0 hit from the other side: Roswaal writes LF, Git
# checked the generated file out as CRLF, and every generated file was then
# reported as edited by hand.
notices/upstream/*.txt -text
